{"repositoryId":1303595982,"availability":"available","full":"hdia/cleancharge-live","name":"cleancharge-live","description":"Real-time carbon-aware EV charging forecasts, evaluation and performance monitoring for Victoria, Australia.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-17T05:24:19Z","updated":"2026-10-17T20:53:24Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://cleancharge-live.streamlit.app/","topics":["carbon-intensity","electric-vehicles","ev-charging","melbourne","open-data","streamlit","sustainable-transport"],"demo":"https://cleancharge-live.streamlit.app/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T15:46:20.385Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T15:46:20.385Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T15:46:20.385Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-18T15:46:20.385Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Daily carbon-aware electric vehicle charging guidance for Victoria, Australia.","CleanCharge Live is an operational research and decision-support platform. It retrieves recent Victorian electricity-system data, maintains a rolling observation history, forecasts regional grid carbon intensity, publishes one lower-carbon charging period for a representative electric vehicle charging scenario, and evaluates its own performance as actual observations become available.","It is the live operational companion to the published CleanCharge research toolkit."],"features":["retrieves hourly Victorian electricity and emissions data from OpenElectricity","maintains a rolling 90-day observation history with coverage checks","forecasts regional electricity carbon intensity for the next operational day","publishes one model-selected lower-carbon charging period for a representative charging scenario","archives each formally published daily forecast without overwriting it"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hdia/cleancharge-live/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f4a154c